nces in subcategories\u003C/em\u003E, J. Algebra \u003Cstrong\u003E69\u003C/strong\u003E (1981), no.\u0026nbsp;2, 426\u0026ndash;454.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=617088\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E617088\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-8693%2881%2990214-3\u0022\u003E10.1016/0021-8693(81)90214-3\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Auslander%2C%20Maurice\u0022\u003EMaurice Auslander\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003ERepresentation dimension of Artin algebras\u003C/em\u003E, Lecture Notes, Queen Mary College, 1971.\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Auslander%2C%20Maurice\u0022\u003EMaurice Auslander\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EFunctors and morphisms determined by objects\u003C/em\u003E, Representation theory of algebras (Proc. Conf., Temple Univ., Philadelphia, Pa., 1976) Lect. Notes Pure Appl. Math., Vol. 37, Dekker, New York-Basel, 1978, pp.\u0026nbsp;1\u0026ndash;244.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=480688\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E480688\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Auslander%2C%20Maurice\u0022\u003EMaurice Auslander\u003C/a\u003E and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Reiten%2C%20Idun\u0022\u003EIdun Reiten\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EOn a theorem of E. Green on the dual of the transpose\u003C/em\u003E, Representations of finite-dimensional algebras (Tsukuba, 1990), 1991, pp.\u0026nbsp;53\u0026ndash;65.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1143845\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1143845\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href