ion: Munakata, Fukuoka, Japan\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMR Author ID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?mrauthid=170685\u0027\u003E170685\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EEmail: ttanisaki@icloud.com\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EReceived by editor(s): February 20, 2022\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EReceived by editor(s) in revised form: August 30, 2022, March 10, 2026, and April 21, 2026\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EPublished electronically: July 16, 2026\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u0026copy; Copyright 2026\nAmerican Mathematical Society\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EJournal: J. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E40\u003C/strong\u003E (2027), 129-193\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMSC (2020): Primary 20G42; Secondary 17B37\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EDOI: https://doi.org/10.1090/jams/1078\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E","PdfUrl":"/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01078-8/S0894-0347-2026-01078-8.pdf","HtmlUrl":"/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01078-8/viewer","Authors":[{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"Toshiyuki Tanisaki","FirstName":"Toshiyuki","MiddleName":" ","LastName":"Tanisaki","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":"TNTSXC","MRAuthorId":170685,"Email":"ttanisaki@icloud.com","CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":"Munakata, Fukuoka, Japan","AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null}],"BookReviews":[],"AMSCopyrightFlag":"Y","CopyrightOwner":"American Mathematical Society","MRNumber":null,"ArticleCitation":"J. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E40\u003C/strong\u003E (2027), 129-193","CrossReferences":"","Abstracts":[],"IsAMSCopyright":true,"PostDateFormatted":"July 16, 2026"},{"ArticleId":93421,"JournalProductCode":"JAMS","IssueId":5822,"ManuscriptId":1081,"DocumentType":"ARTICLE","Title":"Hilbert\u0026rsquo;s tenth problem via additive combinatorics","DOI":"10.1090/jams/1081","PII":"S0894-0347-2026-01081-8","Issue":null,"IssueDirectory":"2027-40-01","StartPage":195,"EndPage":234,"PostDate":"2026-08-10T00:00:00","PrimaryMsc":"11G05, 03D35, 03D25, 11D99","SecondaryMsc":null,"MscSchema":"2020","Abstract":"For all infinite rings $R$ that are finitely generated over $\\mathbb {Z}$, we show that Hilbert\u0026rsquo;s tenth problem has a negative answer. This is accomplished by constructing elliptic curves $E$ without rank growth in certain quadratic extensions $L/K$. To achieve such a result unconditionally, our key innovation is to combine techniques from additive combinatorics with $2$-descent.","EnhancedReferences":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Alpoge%2C%20Levent\u0022\u003ELevent Alp\u0026ouml;ge\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Bhargava%2C%20Manjul\u0022\u003EManjul Bhargava\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Ho%2C%20Wei\u0022\u003EWei Ho\u003C/a\u003E, and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Shnidman%2C%20Ari\u0022\u003EAri Shnidman\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003ERank stability in quadratic extensions and Hilbert\u0026rsquo;s tenth problem for the ring of integers of a number field\u003C/em\u003E, Invent. Math. \u003Cstrong\u003E243\u003C/strong\u003E (2026), no.\u0026nbsp;3, 1129\u0026ndash;1139.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=5008163\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E5008163\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/s00222-025-01392-3\u0022\u003E10.1007/s00222-025-01392-3\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Cesnavicius%2C%20Kestutis\u0022\u003EK\u0026#x119;stutis \u0026#x10C;esnavi\u0026#x10D;ius\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EThe $p$-parity conjecture for elliptic curves with a $p$-isogeny\u003C/em\u003E, J. Reine Angew. Math. \u003Cstrong\u003E719\u003C/strong\u003E (2016), 45\u0026ndash;73.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=3552491\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E3552491\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1515/crelle-2014-0040\u0022\u003E10.1515/crelle-2014-0040\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Cornelissen%2C%20Gunther\u0022\u003EGunther Cornelissen\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Pheidas%2C%20Thanases\u0022\u003EThanases Pheidas\u003C/a\u003E, and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Zahidi%2C%20Karim\u0022\u003EKarim Zahidi\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EDivision-ample sets and the Diophantine problem for rings of integers\u003C/em\u003E, J. Th\u0026eacute;or. Nombres Bordeaux \u003Cstrong\u003E17\u003C/strong\u003E (2005), no.\u0026nbsp;3, 727\u0026ndash;735 (English, with English and French summaries).  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2212121\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2212121\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.5802/jtnb.516\u0022\u003E10.5802/jtnb.516\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Cowland%20Kellock%2C%20Lilybelle\u0022\u003ELilybelle Cowland Kellock\u003C/a\u003E and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Dokchitser%2C%20Vladimir\u0022\u003EVladimir Dokchitser\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003ERoot numbers and parity phenomena\u003C/em\u003E, Bull. Lond. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E55\u003C/strong\u003E (2023), no.\u0026nbsp;6, 2557\u0026ndash;2597.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org