26.0_{1}\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Adam Morgan and Ross Paterson, \u003Cem\u003EOn 2-Selmer groups of twists after quadratic extension\u003C/em\u003E, J. Lond. Math. Soc. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E105\u003C/strong\u003E (2022), no. 2, 1110\u0026ndash;1166. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4400944\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4400944\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1112/jlms.12533\u0022\u003E10.1112/jlms.12533\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E M. Ram Murty and Hector Pasten, \u003Cem\u003EElliptic curves, $L$-functions, and Hilbert\u0026rsquo;s tenth problem\u003C/em\u003E, J. Number Theory \u003Cstrong\u003E182\u003C/strong\u003E (2018), 1\u0026ndash;18. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=3703929\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E3703929\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jnt.2017.07.008\u0022\u003E10.1016/j.jnt.2017.07.008\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E J\u0026uuml;rgen Neukirch, Alexander Schmidt, and Kay Wingberg, \u003Cem\u003ECohomology of number fields\u003C/em\u003E, 2nd ed., Grundlehren der mathematischen Wissenschaften [Fundamental Principles of Mathematical Sciences], vol.\u0026nbsp;323, Springer-Verlag, Berlin, 2008. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2392026\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2392026\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-37889-1\u0022\u003E10.1007/978-3-540-37889-1\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E H. Pasten, \u003Cem\u003ESuperficies el\u0026iacute;pticas y el d\u0026eacute;cimo problema de Hilbert\u003C/em\u003E, Rev. Mat. Teor. Apl. \u003Cstrong\u003E30\u003C/strong\u003E (2023), no. 1, 113\u0026ndash;120.\n\u003Cli\u003E Thanases Pheidas, \u003Cem\u003EHilbert\u0026rsquo;s tenth problem for a class of rings of algebraic integers\u003C/em\u0