                                            <div class="accordion-body">
                  
                                                <span id="lblDescription" class="productDetailDescription"><div>The Journal of the American Mathematical Society publishes articles of exceptional quality and broad interest in all areas of mathematics. We seek articles distinguished not only by the importance of their results but also by the originality of the ideas behind them. We especially welcome papers that open new directions for research and that mathematicians want to read and discuss. <br/><br/></div> <div>Published quarterly since 1988, the Journal is recognized for high impact and uniquely rigorous peer review. <br/><br/></div> <div><span id="issn">ISSN 1088-6834 (online) ISSN 0894-0347 (print)</span><br/><br/></div> <div>The 2024 MCQ for Journal of the American Mathematical Society is <span class="productDetailMCQ">4.83</span>. <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info" data-bs-toggle="popover" data-bs-html="true" data-bs-trigger="focus" title="What is MCQ?"    data-bs-content="The Mathematical Citation Quotient (MCQ) measures journal impact by looking at citations over a five-year period. <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/journal/profile?groupId=3285' target='_blank'>Subscribers to MathSciNet</a> may click through for more detailed information." tabindex="0" style="cursor:pointer;" ></i></div></span>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>

                                </div>
