.pdf'>PDF</a></div></div><li id='articleContent_93418' data-ams-pii='S0894-0347-2026-01078-8'><div><a class='productDetailTitleLink' href='/JAMS/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01078-8/' onclick='selectArticle("5822","93418", null, true); return false;'>Quantized flag manifolds and non-restricted modules over quantum groups at roots of unity</a></div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/author?authorId=170685' target='_blank'>Toshiyuki Tanisaki</a></div><div>J. Amer. Math. Soc. <strong>40</strong> (2027), 129-193</div><div>DOI: https://doi.org/10.1090/jams/1078</div><div>Published electronically: July 16, 2026</div><div class='productDetailFileLinkContainer right'><div class='productDetailFileLinkWrapper'><a class='productDetailBtn productDetailDownloadPdfButton' target='_blank' onclick='return addTimestampToHref(event, this)' href='https://www.ams.org/journals/jams/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01078-8/viewer'>HTML</a></div><div class='productDetailFileLinkWrapper'><a class='productDetailBtn productDetailDownloadPdfButton' target='_blank' onclick='return addTimestampToHref(event, this)' href='https://www.ams.org/journals/jams/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01078-8/S0894-0347-2026-01078-8.pdf'>PDF</a></div></div><li id='articleContent_93421' data-ams-pii='S0894-0347-2026-01081-8'><div><a class='productDetailTitleLink' href='/JAMS/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01081-8/' onclick='selectArticle("5822","93421", null, true); return false;'>Hilbert’s tenth problem via additive combinatorics</a></div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/author?authorId=1208557' target='_blank'>Peter Koymans</a> and <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/author?authorId=1233159' target='_blank'>Carlo Pagano</a></div><div>J. Amer. Math. Soc. <strong>40</strong> (2027), 195-234</div><div>DOI: https://doi.org/10.1090/jams/1081</div><div>Published electronically: August 10, 2026</div><div class='productDetailFileLinkContainer right'><div class='productDetailFileLinkWrapper'><a class='productDetailBtn productDetailDownloadPdfButton' target='_blank' onclick='return addTimestampToHref(event, this)' href='https://www.ams.org/journals/jams/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01081-8/viewer'>HTML</a></div><div class='productDetailFileLinkWrapper'><a class='productDetailBtn productDetailDownloadPdfButton' target='_blank' onclick='return addTimestampToHref(event, this)' href='https://www.ams.org/journals/jams/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01081-8/S0894-0347-2026-01081-8.pdf'>PDF</a></div></div><li id='articleContent_93419' data-ams-pii='S0894-0347-2026-01080-6'><div><a class='productDetailTitleLink' href='/JAMS/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01080-6/' onclick='selectArticle("5822","93419", null, true); return false;'>The correlation energy of the electron gas in the mean-field regime</a></div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/author?authorId=1533961' target='_blank'>Martin Ravn Christiansen</a>, <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/author?authorId=674655' target='_blank'>Christian Hainzl</a> and <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/author?authorId=850145' target='_blank'>Phan Th&agrave;nh Nam</a></div><div>J. Amer. Math. Soc. <strong>40</strong> (2027), 235-316</div><div>DOI: https://doi.org/10.1090/jams/1080</div><div>Published electronically: July 31, 2026</div><div class='productDetailFileLinkContainer right'><div class='productDetailFileLinkWrapper'><a class='productDetailBtn productDetailDownloadPdfButton' target='_blank' onclick='return addTimestampToHref(event, this)' href='https://www.ams.org/journals/jams/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01080-6/viewer'>HTML</a></div><div class='productDetailFileLinkWrapper'><a class='productDetailBtn productDetailDownloadPdfButton' target='_blank' onclick='return addTimestampToHref(event, this)' href='https://www.ams.org/journals/jams/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01080-6/S0894-0347-2026-01080-6.pdf'>PDF</a></div></div></ul></div>
                                                            <script type="text/javascript">
                                                                if(issueMap != null)
                                                                {
                                                                    issueMap.set('5822', {"IssueId":5822,"ProductCode":null,"Year":2027,"Volume":40,"IssueNumber":1,"IssueDirectory":"2027-40-01","FreeFlag":"N","EndMatterUrl":"/2027-40-01/jams-40-1-print-matter.pdf","FileUrlHost":"https://www.ams.org/journals/jams","HomeUrlHost":"https://pubs.ams.org/jams","DirectFileUrl":"","Articles":[{"ArticleId":93420,"JournalProductCode":"JAMS","IssueId":5822,"ManuscriptId":1079,"DocumentType":"ARTICLE","Title":"The derived Auslander\u0026ndash;Iyama correspondence","DOI":"10.1090/jams/1079","PII":"S0894-0347-2026-01079-X","Issue":null,"IssueDirectory":"2027-40-01","StartPage":1,"EndPage":127,"PostDate":"2026-08-21T00:00:00","PrimaryMsc":"18G80","SecondaryMsc":"18N40","MscSchema":"2020","Abstract":"We work over a perfect field. In this article, given an integer $d\\geq 1$, we establish a bijection between twisted $(d\u002B2)$-periodic algebras and suitable algebraic triangulated categories with a $d\\mathbb {Z}$-cluster tilting object. Furthermore, we show that these triangulated categories admit a unique differential graded enhancement. Our result yields recognition theorems for interesting algebraic triangulated categories, such as the Amiot cluster category of a self-injective quiver with potential in the sense of Herschend and Iyama and, more generally, the Amiot\u0026ndash;Guo\u0026ndash;Keller cluster category associated with a $d$-representation finite algebra in the sense of Iyama and Oppermann. As an application of our result, we obtain infinitely many triangulated categories with a unique differential graded enhancement that is not strongly unique. In the appendix, B. Keller explains how\u0026mdash;combined with crucial results of August and Hua\u0026ndash;Keller\u0026mdash;our main result yields the last key ingredient to prove the Donovan\u0026ndash;Wemyss Conjecture in the context of the Homological Minimal Model Program for threefolds.","EnhancedReferences":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Aihara%2C%20Takuma\u0022\u003ETakuma Aihara\u003C/a\u003E and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Iyama%2C%20Osamu\u0022\u003EOsamu Iyama\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003ESilting mutation in triangulated categories\u003C/em\u003E, J. Lond. Math. Soc. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E85\u003C/strong\u003E (2012), no.\u0026nbsp;3, 633\u0026ndash;668.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2927802\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2927802\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1112/jlms/jdr055\u0022\u003E10.1112/jlms/jdr055\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Amiot%2C%20Claire\u0022\u003EClaire Amiot\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EOn the structure of triangulated categories with finitely many indecomposables\u003C/em\u003E, Bull. Soc. Math. France \u003Cstrong\u003E135\u003C/strong\u003E (2007), no.\u0026nbsp;3, 435\u0026ndash;474 (English, with English and French summaries).  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2430189\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2430189\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.24033/bsmf.2542\u0022\u003E10.24033/bsmf.2542\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Amiot%2C%20Claire\u0022\u003EClaire Amiot\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003ESur les petites cat\u0026eacute;gories triangul\u0026eacute;es\u003C/em\u003E, Ph.D. Thesis, Universit\u0026eacute; Paris 7, 2008.\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Amiot%2C%20Claire\u0022\u003EClaire Amiot\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003ECluster categories for algebras of global dimension 2 and quivers with potential\u003C/em\u003E, Ann. Inst. Fourier (Grenoble) \u003Cstrong\u003E59\u003C/strong\u003E (2009), no.\u0026nbsp;6, 2525\u0026ndash;2590 (English, with English and French summaries).  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2640929\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2640929\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.5802/aif.2499\u0022\u003E10.5802/aif.2499\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Angeltveit%2C%20Vigleik\u0022\u003EVigleik Angeltveit\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EUniqueness of Morava $K$-theory\u003C/em\u003E, Compos. Math. \u003Cstrong\u003E147\u003C/strong\u003E (2011), no.\u0026nbsp;2, 633\u0026ndash;648.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2776615\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2776615\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1112/S0010437X10005026\u0022\u003E10.1112/S0010437X10005026\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Antieau%2C%20Benjamin\u0022\u003EBenjamin Antieau\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EOn the uniqueness of infinity-categorical enhancements of triangulated categories\u003C/em\u003E,  arXiv:\u003Ca href=\u0022https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.01526\u0022\u003E1812.01526\u003C/a\u003E.\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=August%2C%20Jenny\u0022\u003EJenny August\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EThe tilting theory of contraction algebras\u003C/em\u003E, Adv. Math. \u003Cstrong\u003E374\u003C/strong\u003E (2020), 107372, 56.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4157576\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4157576\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2020.107372\u0022\u003E10.1016/j.aim.2020.107372\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=August%2C%20Jenny\u0022\u003EJenny August\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EOn the finiteness of the derived equivalence classes of some stable endomorphism rings\u003C/em\u003E, Math. Z. \u003Cstrong\u003E296\u003C/strong\u003E (2020), no.\u0026nbsp;3-4, 1157\u0026ndash;1183.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4159827\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4159827\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/s00209-020-02475-y\u0022\u003E10.1007/s00209-020-02475-y\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Auslander%2C%20M.\u0022\u003EM. Auslander\u003C/a\u003E and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Smalo%2C%20Sverre%20O.\u0022\u003ESverre\u0026nbsp;O. Smal\u0026oslash;\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EPreprojective modules over Artin algebras\u003C/em\u003E, J. Algebra \u003Cstrong\u003E66\u003C/strong\u003E (1980), no.\u0026nbsp;1, 61\u0026ndash;122.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=591246\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E591246\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-8693%2880%2990113-1\u0022\u003E10.1016/0021-8693(80)90113-1\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Auslander%2C%20M.\u0022\u003EM. Auslander\u003C/a\u003E and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Smalo%2C%20Sverre%20O.\u0022\u003ESverre O. Smal\u0026oslash;\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EAlmost split sequences in subcategories\u003C/em\u003E, J. Algebra \u003Cstrong\u003E69\u003C/strong\u003E (1981), no.\u0026nbsp;2, 426\u0026ndash;454.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=617088\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E617088\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-8693%2881%2990214-3\u0022\u003E10.1016/0021-8693(81)90214-3\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Auslander%2C%20Maurice\u0022\u003EMaurice Auslander\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003ERepresentation dimension of Artin algebras\u003C/em\u003E, Lecture Notes, Queen Mary College, 1971.\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Auslander%2C%20Maurice\u0022\u003EMaurice Auslander\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EFunctors and morphisms determined by objects\u003C/em\u003E, Representation theory of algebras (Proc. Conf., Temple Univ., Philadelphia, Pa., 1976) Lect. Notes Pure Appl. Math., Vol. 37, Dekker, New York-Basel, 1978, pp.\u0026nbsp;1\u0026ndash;244.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=480688\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E480688\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Auslander%2C%20Maurice\u0022\u003EMaurice Auslander\u003C/a\u003E and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Reiten%2C%20Idun\u0022\u003EIdun Reiten\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EOn a theorem of E. Green on the dual of the transpose\u003C/em\u003E, Representations of finite-dimensional algebras (Tsukuba, 1990), 1991, pp.\u0026nbsp;53\u0026ndash;65.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1143845\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1143845\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1016/0001-8708%2891%2990037-8\u0022\u003E10.1016/0001