:93419,"JournalProductCode":"JAMS","IssueId":5822,"ManuscriptId":1080,"DocumentType":"ARTICLE","Title":"The correlation energy of the electron gas in the mean-field regime","DOI":"10.1090/jams/1080","PII":"S0894-0347-2026-01080-6","Issue":null,"IssueDirectory":"2027-40-01","StartPage":235,"EndPage":316,"PostDate":"2026-07-31T00:00:00","PrimaryMsc":"81V74","SecondaryMsc":null,"MscSchema":"2020","Abstract":"We prove a rigorous lower bound on the correlation energy of interacting fermions in the mean-field regime for a wide class of singular interactions, including the Coulomb potential. Combined with the upper bound obtained by Christiansen, Hainzl, and Nam [Comm. Math. Phys. 401 (2023), pp. 1469\u0026ndash;1529], our result establishes an analogue of the Gell-Mann\u0026ndash;Brueckner formula $c_{1}\\rho \\log \\left (\\rho \\right )\u002Bc_{2}\\rho$ for the correlation energy of the electron gas in the high-density limit. Moreover, our analysis allows us to go beyond mean-field scaling while still covering the same class of potentials.","EnhancedReferences":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Bach%2C%20Volker\u0022\u003EVolker Bach\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EError bound for the Hartree-Fock energy of atoms and molecules\u003C/em\u003E, Comm. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E147\u003C/strong\u003E (1992), no.\u0026nbsp;3, 527\u0026ndash;548.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1175492\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1175492\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02097241\u0022\u003E10.1007/BF02097241\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Boccato%2C%20Chiara\u0022\u003EChiara Boccato\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Brennecke%2C%20Christian\u0022\u003EChristian Brennecke\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Cenatiempo%2C%20Serena\u0022\u003ESerena Cenatiempo\u003C/a\u003E, and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Schlein%2C%20Benjamin\u0022\u003EBenjamin Schlein\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EBogoliubov theory in the Gross-Pitaevskii limit\u003C/em\u003E, Acta Math. \u003Cstrong\u003E222\u003C/strong\u003E (2019), no.\u0026nbsp;2, 219\u0026ndash;335.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=3974476\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E3974476\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.4310/ACTA.2019.v222.n2.a1\u0022\u003E10.4310/ACTA.2019.v222.n2.a1\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Benedikter%2C%20Niels\u0022\u003ENiels Benedikter\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Nam%2C%20Phan%20Thanh\u0022\u003EPhan Th\u0026agrave;nh Nam\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Porta%2C%20Marcello\u0022\u003EMarcello Porta\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Schlein%2C%20Benjamin\u0022\u003EBenjamin Schlein\u003C/a\u003E, and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Seiringer%2C%20Robert\u0022\u003ERobert Seiringer\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EOptimal upper bound for the correlation energy of a Fermi gas in the mean-field regime\u003C/em\u003E, Comm. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E374\u003C/strong\u003E (2020), no.\u0026nbsp;3, 2097\u0026ndash;2150.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4076094\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4076094\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u