tron interactions. III. Coulomb interactions in a degenerate electron gas\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E92\u003C/strong\u003E (1953), 609\u0026ndash;625. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=102332\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E102332\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E J. Bourgain, Z. Rudnick, and P. Sarnak, \u003Cem\u003ESpatial statistics for lattice points on the sphere I: Individual results\u003C/em\u003E, Bull. Iranian Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E43\u003C/strong\u003E (2017), no. 4, 361\u0026ndash;386. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=3711836\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E3711836\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Morris Brooks, \u003Cem\u003EDiagonalizing Bose gases in the Gross-Pitaevskii regime and beyond\u003C/em\u003E, Comm. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E406\u003C/strong\u003E (2025), no. 1, Paper No. 17, 59. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4841753\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4841753\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-024-05199-w\u0022\u003E10.1007/s00220-024-05199-w\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Martin Ravn Christiansen, Christian Hainzl, and Phan Th\u0026agrave;nh Nam, \u003Cem\u003EThe random phase approximation for interacting Fermi gases in the mean-field regime\u003C/em\u003E, Forum Math. Pi \u003Cstrong\u003E11\u003C/strong\u003E (2023), Paper No. e32, 131. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4681199\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4681199\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1017/fmp.2023.31\u0022\u003E10.1017/fmp.2023.31\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Martin Ravn Christiansen, Christian Hainzl, and Phan Th\u0026agrave;nh Nam, \u003Cem\u003EThe Gell-Mann\u0026ndash;Brueckner formula for the correlation energy of the electron gas: a rigorous upper bound in the mean-field regime\u003C/em\u003E, Comm. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E401\u003C/strong\u003E (2023), no. 2, 1469\u0026ndash;1529. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4610280\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4610280\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-023-04672-2\u0022\u003E10.1007/s00220-023-04672-2\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Freeman J. Dyson and A. Lenard, \u003Cem\u003EStability of matter. I\u003C/em\u003E, J. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E8\u003C/strong\u003E (1967), no. 3, 423\u0026ndash;434. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2408896\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2408896\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1705209\u0022\u003E10.1063/1.1705209\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Charles L. Fefferman and Luis A. Seco, \u003Cem\u003EOn the energy of a large atom\u003C/em\u003E, Bull. Amer. Math. Soc. (N.S.) \u003Cstrong\u003E23\u003C/strong\u003E (1990), no. 2, 525\u0026ndash;530. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1056556\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1056556\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1090/S0273-0979-1990-15969-5\u0022\u003E10.1090/S0273-0979-1990-15969-5\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E S\u0026oslash;ren Fournais, B\u0026#x142;a\u0026#x17C;ej Ruba, and Jan Philip Solovej, \u003Cem\u003EGround state energy of dense gases of strongly interacting fermions\u003C/em\u003E, Ann. Henri Poincar\u0026eacute; \u003Cstrong\u003E26\u003C/strong\u003E (2025), no. 8, 3007\u0026ndash;3027. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4940129\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4940129\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/s00023-024-01506-2\u0022\u003E10.1007/s00023-024-01506-2\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E S\u0026oslash;ren Fournais and Jan Philip Solovej, \u003Cem\u003EThe energy of dilute Bose gases\u003C/em\u003E, Ann. of Math. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E192\u003C/strong\u003E (2020), no. 3, 893\u0026ndash;976. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4172623\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4172623\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.4007/annals.2020.192.3.5\u0022\u003E10.4007/annals.2020.192.3.5\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Murray Gell-Mann and Keith A. Brueckner, \u003Cem\u003ECorrelation energy of an electron gas at high density\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E106\u003C/strong\u003E (1957), 364\u0026ndash;368. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=85896\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E85896\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E D. Gontier, C. Hainzl, and M. Lewin, \u003Cem\u003ELower bound on the Hartree-Fock energy of the electron gas\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. A \u003Cstrong\u003E99\u003C/strong\u003E (2019), 052501.\n\u003Cli\u003E Gian Michele Graf and Jan Philip Solovej, \u003Cem\u003EA correlation estimate with applications to quantum systems with Coulomb interactions\u003C/em\u003E, Rev. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E6\u003C/strong\u003E (1994), no. 5A, 977\u0026ndash;997. Special issue dedicated to Elliott H. Lieb. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1301362\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1301362\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X94000328\u0022\u003E10.1142/S0129055X94000328\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Christian Hainzl, Marcello Porta, and Felix Rexze, \u003Cem\u003EOn the correlation energy of interacting fermionic systems in the mean-field regime\u003C/em\u003E, Comm. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E374\u003C/strong\u003E (2020), no. 2, 485\u0026ndash;524. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4072222\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4072222\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-019-03654-7\u0022\u003E10.1007/s00220-019-03654-7\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E W. Heisenberg, \u003Cem\u003EZur Theorie der Supraleitung\u003C/em\u003E, Z. Naturforschung A, \u003Cstrong\u003E2\u003C/strong\u003E (1947), no. 4, 185\u0026ndash;201.\n\u003Cli\u003E J. L. Lebowitz and E. H. Lieb, \u003Cem\u003EExistence of thermodynamics for real matter with Coulomb forces\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. Lett. \u003Cstrong\u003E22\u003C/strong\u003E (1969), 631\u0026ndash;634.\n\u003Cli\u003E Elliott H. Lieb and Heide Narnhofer, \u003Cem\u003EThe thermodynamic limit for jellium\u003C/em\u003E, J. Statist. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E12\u003C/strong\u003E (1975), 291\u0026ndash;310. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=401029\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E401029\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01012066\u0022\u003E10.1007/BF01012066\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Elliott H. Lieb and Jan Philip Solovej, \u003Cem\u003EGround state energy of the one-component charged Bose gas\u003C/em\u003E, Comm. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E217\u003C/strong\u003E (2001), no. 1, 127\u0026ndash;163. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1815028\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1815028\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/s002200000353\u0022\u003E10.1007/s002200000353\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E E. H. Lieb and W. Thirring, \u003Cem\u003EBound for the kinetic energy of fermions which proves the stability of matter\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. Lett. \u003Cstrong\u003E35\u003C/strong\u003E (1975), 687\u0026ndash;689.\n\u003Cli\u003E W. Macke, \u003Cem\u003E\u0026Uuml;ber die Wechselwirkungen im Fermi-Gas. Polarisationserscheinungen, Correlationsenergie, Elektronenkondensation\u003C/em\u003E, Z. Naturforschung A, \u003Cstrong\u003E5\u003C/strong\u003E (1950), no. 4, 192\u0026ndash;208.\n\u003Cli\u003E D. Pines, \u003Cem\u003EA collective description of electron interactions: IV. Electron interaction in metals\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E92\u003C/strong\u003E (1953), 626.\n\u003Cli\u003E Katuro Sawada, \u003Cem\u003ECorrelation energy of an electron gas at high density\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E106\u003C/strong\u003E (1957), 372\u0026ndash;383. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=85898\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E85898\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E K. Sawada, K. A. Brueckner, N. Fukuda, and R. Brout, \u003Cem\u003ECorrelation energy of an electron gas at high density. Plasma oscillations\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E108\u003C/strong\u003E (1957), 507\u0026ndash;514. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=107525\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E107525\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E E. Wigner, \u003Cem\u003EOn the interaction of electrons in metals\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E46\u003C/strong\u003E (1934), no, 11, 1002\u0026ndash; 1011.\n\u003C/ul\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E","BibliographicInfo":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EMartin Ravn Christiansen\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EAffiliation: Department of Mathematics, Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich, Germany\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMR Author ID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?mrauthid=1533961\u0027\u003E1533961\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EEmail: martin.christiansen@math.lmu.de\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EChristian Hainzl\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EAffiliation: Department of Mathematics, Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich, Germany\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMR Author ID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?mrauthid=674655\u0027\u003E674655\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EEmail: hainzl@math.lmu.de\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPhan Th\u0026agrave;nh Nam\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EAffiliation: Department of Mathematics, Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich, Germany\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMR Author ID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?mrauthid=850145\u0027\u003E850145\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EORCID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7599-9742\u0027\u003E0000-0001-7599-9742\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EEmail: nam@math.lmu.de\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EReceived by editor(s): May 6, 2024\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EReceived by editor(s) in revised form: February 9, 2026, and May 1, 2026\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EPublished electronically: July 31, 2026\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EAdditional Notes: This work was partially funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research Foundation) via the TRR 352 \u2013 Project-ID 470903074. The third author was partially supported by the European Research Council via the ERC CoG RAMBAS \u2013 Project-Nr. 101044249.\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u0026copy; Copyright 2026\nby the authors\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EJournal: J. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E40\u003C/strong\u003E (2027), 235-316\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMSC (2020): Primary 81V74\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EDOI: https://doi.org/10.1090/jams/1080\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E","PdfUrl":"/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01080-6/S0894-0347-2026-01080-6.pdf","HtmlUrl":"/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01080-6/viewer","Authors":[{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"Martin Ravn Christiansen","FirstName":"Martin Ravn","MiddleName":" ","LastName":"Christiansen","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":"RVMRXR","MRAuthorId":1533961,"Email":"martin.christiansen@math.lmu.de","CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":"Department of Mathematics, Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich, Germany","AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null},{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"Christian Hainzl","FirstName":"Christian","MiddleName":" ","LastName":"Hainzl","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":"HNCHXNA","MRAuthorId":674655,"Email":"hainzl@math.lmu.de","CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":"Department of Mathematics, Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich, Germany","AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null},{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"Phan Th\u0026agrave;nh Nam","FirstName":"Phan","MiddleName":"Th\u0026agrave;nh","LastName":"Nam","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":"NMPHTA","MRAuthorId":850145,"Email":"nam@math.lmu.de","CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":"Department of Mathematics, Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich, Germany","AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null}],"BookReviews":[],"AMSCopyrightFlag":"N","CopyrightOwner":"by the authors","MRNumber":null,"ArticleCitation":"J. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E40\u003C/strong\u003E (2027), 235-316","CrossReferences":"","Abstracts":[],"IsAMSCopyright":false,"PostDateFormatted":"July 31, 2026"}]});

