tron gas: a rigorous upper bound in the mean-field regime\u003C/em\u003E, Comm. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E401\u003C/strong\u003E (2023), no. 2, 1469\u0026ndash;1529. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4610280\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4610280\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-023-04672-2\u0022\u003E10.1007/s00220-023-04672-2\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Freeman J. Dyson and A. Lenard, \u003Cem\u003EStability of matter. I\u003C/em\u003E, J. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E8\u003C/strong\u003E (1967), no. 3, 423\u0026ndash;434. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2408896\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2408896\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1705209\u0022\u003E10.1063/1.1705209\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Charles L. Fefferman and Luis A. Seco, \u003Cem\u003EOn the energy of a large atom\u003C/em\u003E, Bull. Amer. Math. Soc. (N.S.) \u003Cstrong\u003E23\u003C/strong\u003E (1990), no. 2, 525\u0026ndash;530. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1056556\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1056556\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1090/S0273-0979-1990-15969-5\u0022\u003E10.1090/S0273-0979-1990-15969-5\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E S\u0026oslash;ren Fournais, B\u0026#x142;a\u0026#x17C;ej Ruba, and Jan Philip Solovej, \u003Cem\u003EGround state energy of dense gases of strongly interacting fermions\u003C/em\u003E, Ann. Henri Poincar\u0026eacute; \u003Cstrong\u003E26\u003C/strong\u003E (2025), no. 8, 3007\u0026ndash;3027. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4940129\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4940129\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/s00023-024-01506-2\u0022\u003E10.1007/s00023-024-01506-2\u003C/a\u003