risationserscheinungen, Correlationsenergie, Elektronenkondensation\u003C/em\u003E, Z. Naturforschung A, \u003Cstrong\u003E5\u003C/strong\u003E (1950), no. 4, 192\u0026ndash;208.\n\u003Cli\u003E D. Pines, \u003Cem\u003EA collective description of electron interactions: IV. Electron interaction in metals\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E92\u003C/strong\u003E (1953), 626.\n\u003Cli\u003E Katuro Sawada, \u003Cem\u003ECorrelation energy of an electron gas at high density\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E106\u003C/strong\u003E (1957), 372\u0026ndash;383. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=85898\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E85898\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E K. Sawada, K. A. Brueckner, N. Fukuda, and R. Brout, \u003Cem\u003ECorrelation energy of an electron gas at high density. Plasma oscillations\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E108\u003C/strong\u003E (1957), 507\u0026ndash;514. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=107525\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E107525\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E E. Wigner, \u003Cem\u003EOn the interaction of electrons in metals\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E46\u003C/strong\u003E (1934), no, 11, 1002\u0026ndash; 1011.\n\u003C/ul\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E","BibliographicInfo":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EMartin Ravn Christiansen\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EAffiliation: Department of Mathematics, Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich, Germany\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMR Author ID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?mrauthid=1533961\u0027\u003E1533961\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EEmail: martin.christiansen@math.lmu.de\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EChristian Hainzl\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EAffiliation: Department of Mathematics, Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich, Germany\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMR Author ID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?mrauthid=674655\u0027\u003E674655\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EEmail: hainzl@math.lmu.de\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPhan Th\u0026agrave;nh Nam\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EAffiliation: Department of Mathematics, Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich, Germany\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMR Author ID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?mrauthid=850145\u0027\u003E850145\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EORCID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7599-9742\u0027\u003E0000-0001-7599-9742\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EEmail: nam@math.lmu.de\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EReceived by editor(s): May 6, 2024\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EReceived by editor(s) in revised form: February 9, 2026, and May 1, 2026\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EPublished electronically: July 31, 2026\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EAdditional Notes: This work was partially funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research Foundation) via the TRR 352 \u2013 Project-ID 470903074. The third author was partially supported by the European Research Council via the ERC CoG RAMBAS \u2013 Project-Nr. 101044249.\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u0026copy; Copyright 2026\nby the authors\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EJournal: J. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E40\u003C/strong\u003E (2027), 235-316\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMSC (2020): Primary 81V74\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EDOI: https://doi.org/10.1090/jams/1080\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E","PdfUrl":"/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01080-6/S0894-0347-2026-01080-6.pdf","HtmlUrl":"/2027-40-01/S0894-0347-2026-01080-6/viewer","Authors":[{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"Martin Ravn Christiansen","FirstName":"Martin Ravn","MiddleName":" ","LastName":"Christiansen","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":"RVMRXR","MRAuthorId":1533961,"Email":"martin.christiansen@math.lmu.de","CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":"Department of Mathematics, Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich, Germany","AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null},{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"Christian Hainzl","FirstName":"Christian","MiddleName":" ","LastName":"Hainzl","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":"HNCHXNA","MRAuthorId":674655,"Email":"hainzl@math.lmu.de","CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":"Department of Mathematics, Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich, Germany","AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null},{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"Phan Th\u0026agrave;nh Nam","FirstName":"Phan","MiddleName":"Th\u0026agrave;nh","LastName":"Nam","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":"NMPHTA","MRAuthorId":850145,"Email":"nam@math.lmu.de","CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":"Department of Mathematics, Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich, Germany","AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null}],"BookReviews":[],"AMSCopyrightFlag":"N","CopyrightOwner":"by the authors","MRNumber":null,"ArticleCitation":"J. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E40\u003C/strong\u003E (2027), 235-316","CrossReferences":"","Abstracts":[],"IsAMSCopyright":false,"PostDateFormatted":"July 31, 2026"}]}, [{"ArticleId":93420,"JournalProductCode":"JAMS","IssueId":5822,"ManuscriptId":1079,"DocumentType":"ARTICLE","Title":"The derived Auslander\u0026ndash;Iyama correspondence","DOI":"10.1090/jams/1079","PII":"S0894-0347-2026-01079-X","Issue":null,"IssueDirectory":"2027-40-01","StartPage":1,"EndPage":127,"PostDate":"2026-08-21T00:00:00","PrimaryMsc":"18G80","SecondaryMsc":"18N40","MscSchema":"2020","Abstract":"We work over a perfect field. In this article, given an integer $d\\geq 1$, we establish a bijection between twisted $(d\u002B2)$-periodic algebras and suitable algebraic triangulated categories with a $d\\mathbb {Z}$-cluster tilting object. Furthermore, we show that these triangulated categories admit a unique differential graded enhancement. Our result yields recognition theorems for interesting algebraic triangulated categories, such as the Amiot cluster category of a self-injective quiver with potential in the sense of Herschend and Iyama and, more generally, the Amiot\u0026ndash;Guo\u0026ndash;Keller cluster category associated with a $d$-representation finite algebra in the sense of Iyama and Oppermann. As an application of our result, we obtain infinitely many triangulated categories with a unique differential graded enhancement that is not strongly unique. In the appendix, B. Keller explains how\u0026mdash;combined with crucial results of August and Hua\u0026ndash;Keller\u0026mdash;our main result yields the last key ingredient to prove the Donovan\u0026ndash;Wemyss Conjecture in the context of the Homological Minimal Model Program for threefolds.","EnhancedReferences":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Aihara%2C%20Takuma\u0022\u003ETakuma Aihara\u003C/a\u003E and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Iyama%2C%20Osamu\u0022\u003EOsamu Iyama\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003ESilting mutation in triangulated categories\u003C/em\u003E, J. Lond. Math. Soc. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E85\u003C/strong\u003E (2012), no.\u0026nbsp;3, 633\u0026ndash;668.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2927802\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2927802\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1112/jlms/jdr055\u0022\u003E10.1112/jlms/jdr055\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Amiot%2C%20Claire\u0022\u003EClaire Amiot\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EOn the structure of triangulated categories with finitely many indecomposables\u003C/em\u003E, Bull. Soc. Math. France \u003Cstrong\u003E135\u003C/strong\u003E (2007), no.\u0026nbsp;3, 435\u0026ndash;474 (English, with English and French summaries).  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2430189\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2430189\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.24033/bsmf.2542\u0022\u003E10.24033/bsmf.2542\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Amiot%2C%20Claire\u0022\u003EClaire Amiot\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003ESur les petites cat\u0026eacute;gories triangul\u0026eacute;es\u003C/em\u003E, Ph.D. Thesis, Universit\u0026eacute; Paris 7, 2008.\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Amiot%2C%20Claire\u0022\u003EClaire Amiot\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003ECluster categories for algebras of global dimension 2 and quivers with potential\u003C/em\u003E, Ann. Inst. Fourier (Grenoble) \u003Cstrong\u003E59\u003C/strong\u003E (2009), no.\u0026nbsp;6, 2525\u0026ndash;2590 (English, with English and French summaries).  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2640929\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2640929\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.5802/aif.2499\u0022\u003E10.5802/aif.2499\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Angeltveit%2C%20Vigleik\u0022\u003EVigleik Angeltveit\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EUniqueness of Morava $K$-theory\u003C/em\u003E, Compos. Math. \u003Cstrong\u003E147\u003C/strong\u003E (2011), no.\u0026nbsp;2, 633\u0026ndash;648.  \u00