133\u0022\u003E10.2307/1998133\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E J. Denef and L. Lipshitz, \u003Cem\u003EDiophantine sets over some rings of algebraic integers\u003C/em\u003E, J. London Math. Soc. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E18\u003C/strong\u003E (1978), no. 3, 385\u0026ndash;391. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=518221\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E518221\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1112/jlms/s2-18.3.385\u0022\u003E10.1112/jlms/s2-18.3.385\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Tim Dokchitser and Vladimir Dokchitser, \u003Cem\u003EOn the Birch-Swinnerton-Dyer quotients modulo squares\u003C/em\u003E, Ann. of Math. (2) \u003Cstrong\u003E172\u003C/strong\u003E (2010), no. 1, 567\u0026ndash;596. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2680426\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2680426\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.4007/annals.2010.172.567\u0022\u003E10.4007/annals.2010.172.567\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Tim Dokchitser and Vladimir Dokchitser, \u003Cem\u003ERoot numbers and parity of ranks of elliptic curves\u003C/em\u003E, J. Reine Angew. Math. \u003Cstrong\u003E658\u003C/strong\u003E (2011), 39\u0026ndash;64. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2831512\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2831512\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1515/CRELLE.2011.060\u0022\u003E10.1515/CRELLE.2011.060\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Anne Kirsten Eisentraeger, \u003Cem\u003EHilbert\u0026rsquo;s tenth problem and arithmetic geometry\u003C/em\u003E, ProQuest LLC, Ann Arbor, MI, 2003. Thesis (Ph.D.)\u0026ndash;University of California, Berkeley. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2705180\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2705180\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E