UTHOR","FullName":"Peter Koymans","FirstName":"Peter","MiddleName":" ","LastName":"Koymans","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":"KYPTXB","MRAuthorId":1208557,"Email":"p.h.koymans@uu.nl","CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":"Mathematisch Instituut, Universiteit Utrecht, Postbus 80.010, 3508 TA Utrecht, The Netherlands","AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null},{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"Carlo Pagano","FirstName":"Carlo","MiddleName":" ","LastName":"Pagano","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":"PGCRXE","MRAuthorId":1233159,"Email":"carlein90@gmail.com","CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":"Department of Mathematics and Statistics, Montreal, Quebec H3G 1M8, Canada","AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null}],"BookReviews":[],"AMSCopyrightFlag":"Y","CopyrightOwner":"American Mathematical Society","MRNumber":null,"ArticleCitation":"J. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E40\u003C/strong\u003E (2027), 195-234","CrossReferences":"","Abstracts":[],"IsAMSCopyright":true,"PostDateFormatted":"August 10, 2026"},{"ArticleId":93419,"JournalProductCode":"JAMS","IssueId":5822,"ManuscriptId":1080,"DocumentType":"ARTICLE","Title":"The correlation energy of the electron gas in the mean-field regime","DOI":"10.1090/jams/1080","PII":"S0894-0347-2026-01080-6","Issue":null,"IssueDirectory":"2027-40-01","StartPage":235,"EndPage":316,"PostDate":"2026-07-31T00:00:00","PrimaryMsc":"81V74","SecondaryMsc":null,"MscSchema":"2020","Abstract":"We prove a rigorous lower bound on the correlation energy of interacting fermions in the mean-field regime for a wide class of singular interactions, including the Coulomb potential. Combined with the upper bound obtained by Christiansen, Hainzl, and Nam [Comm. Math. Phys. 401 (2023), pp. 1469\u0026ndash;1529], our result establishes an analogue of the Gell-Mann\u0026ndash;Brueckner formula $c_{1}\\rho \\log \\left (\\rho \\right )\u002Bc_{2}\\rho$ for the correlation energy of the electron gas in the high-density limit. Moreover, our analysis allows us to go beyond mean-field scaling while still covering the same class of potentials.","EnhancedReferences":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Bach%2C%20Volker\u0022\u003EVolker Bach\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EError bound for the Hartree-Fock energy of atoms and molecules\u003C/em\u003E, Comm. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E147\u003C/strong\u003E (1992), no.\u0026nbsp;3, 527\u0026ndash;548.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1175492\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1175492\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02097241\u0022\u003E10.1007/BF02097241\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Boccato%2C%20Chiara\u0022\u003EChiara Boccato\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Brennecke%2C%20Christian\u0022\u003EChristian Brennecke\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Cenatiempo%2C%20Serena\u0022\u003ESerena Cenatiempo\u003C/a\u003E, and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Schlein%2C%20Benjamin\u0022\u003EBenjamin Schlein\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EBogoliubov theory in the Gross-Pitaevskii limit\u003C/em\u003E, Acta Math. \u003Cstrong\u003E222\u003C/strong\u003E (2019), no.\u0026nbsp;2, 219\u0026ndash;335.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=3974476\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E3974476\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.4310/ACTA.2019.v222.n2.a1\u0022\u003E10.4310/ACTA.2019.v222.n2.a1\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003