85896\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E85896\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E D. Gontier, C. Hainzl, and M. Lewin, \u003Cem\u003ELower bound on the Hartree-Fock energy of the electron gas\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. A \u003Cstrong\u003E99\u003C/strong\u003E (2019), 052501.\n\u003Cli\u003E Gian Michele Graf and Jan Philip Solovej, \u003Cem\u003EA correlation estimate with applications to quantum systems with Coulomb interactions\u003C/em\u003E, Rev. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E6\u003C/strong\u003E (1994), no. 5A, 977\u0026ndash;997. Special issue dedicated to Elliott H. Lieb. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1301362\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1301362\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X94000328\u0022\u003E10.1142/S0129055X94000328\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Christian Hainzl, Marcello Porta, and Felix Rexze, \u003Cem\u003EOn the correlation energy of interacting fermionic systems in the mean-field regime\u003C/em\u003E, Comm. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E374\u003C/strong\u003E (2020), no. 2, 485\u0026ndash;524. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4072222\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4072222\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-019-03654-7\u0022\u003E10.1007/s00220-019-03654-7\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E W. Heisenberg, \u003Cem\u003EZur Theorie der Supraleitung\u003C/em\u003E, Z. Naturforschung A, \u003Cstrong\u003E2\u003C/strong\u003E (1947), no. 4, 185\u0026ndash;201.\n\u003Cli\u003E J. L. Lebowitz and E. H. Lieb, \u003Cem\u003EExistence of thermodynamics for real matter with Coulomb forces\u003C/em\u003E, Phys. Rev. Lett. \u003Cstrong\u003E22\u003C/strong\u003E (1969), 631\u0026ndash;634.\n\u003Cli\u003E Elliott H. Lieb and Heide Narnhofer, \u003Cem\u003EThe thermodynamic limit for jellium\u003C/em\u003E, J. Statist. Phy