ntegrals\u003C/em\u003E, Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E101\u003C/strong\u003E (1961), 139-167.\nJ. E. Taylor and F. J. Almgren, \u003Cem\u003EOptimal crystal shapes\u003C/em\u003E, Variational Methods for Free Surface Interfaces (P. Concus and R. Finn, eds.), Springer-Verlag, New York, 1987, pp. 1-11.\nG. Talenti, \u003Cem\u003EBest constant in Sobolev inequality\u003C/em\u003E, Ann. Mat. Pura Appl. \u003Cstrong\u003E110\u003C/strong\u003E (1976), 353-372.\nH. Whitney, \u003Cem\u003EA function not constant on a connected set of critical points\u003C/em\u003E, Duke Math. J. \u003Cstrong\u003E1\u003C/strong\u003E (1935), 514-517.\n\u003C/ul\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E","BibliographicInfo":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EFrederick J. Almgren\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EElliott H. Lieb\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u0026copy; Copyright 1989\nAmerican Mathematical Society\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EJournal: J. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E2\u003C/strong\u003E (1989), 683-773\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMSC: Primary 49F20; Secondary 46E30, 49A50\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EDOI: https://doi.org/10.1090/S0894-0347-1989-1002633-4\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMathSciNet review: \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1002633\u0022\u003E1002633\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E","PdfUrl":"/1989-02-04/S0894-0347-1989-1002633-4/S0894-0347-1989-1002633-4.pdf","HtmlUrl":null,"Authors":[{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"Frederick J. Almgren","FirstName":"Frederick J.","MiddleName":" ","LastName":"Almgren","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":" ","MRAuthorId":0,"Email":null,"CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":null,"AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null},{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"Elliott H. Lieb","FirstName":"Elliott H.","MiddleName":" ","LastName":"Lieb","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":" ","MRAuthorId":0,"Email":null,"CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":null,"AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null}],"BookReviews":[],"AMSCopyrightFlag":"Y","CopyrightOwner":"American Mathematical Society","MRNumber":"1002633","ArticleCitation":"J. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E2\u003C/strong\u003E (1989), 683-773","CrossReferences":"","Abstracts":[],"IsAMSCopyright":true,"PostDateFormatted":""},{"ArticleId":17769,"JournalProductCode":"JAMS","IssueId":729,"ManuscriptId":1001850,"DocumentType":"ARTICLE","Title":"Trace rings of generic matrices are Cohen-Macaulay","DOI":"10.1090/S0894-0347-1989-1001850-7","PII":"S0894-0347-1989-1001850-7","Issue":null,"IssueDirectory":"1989-02-04","StartPage":775,"EndPage":799,"PostDate":null,"PrimaryMsc":"14L30","SecondaryMsc":"14M05","MscSchema":null,"Abstract":"In this paper, we prove that trace rings of generic matrics are Cohen-Macaulay (Theorem 7.3.6). This is done by relating this problem to a conjecture of Stanley about modules of invariants under a reductive group. We prove a slightly weakened version (Conjecture 3.4\u2019) of this conjecture in special cases (Theorem 6.1.8). In particular, we obtain that Conjecture 3.4\u2019 is true for $S{L_2}$ (Remark 6.1.10).","EnhancedReferences":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Artin%2C%20M.\u0022\u003EM. Artin\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EOn Azumaya algebras and finite dimensional representations of rings\u003C/em\u003E, J. Algebra \u003Cstrong\u003E11\u003C/strong\u003E (1969), 532\u2013563.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=242890\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E242890\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-8693%2869%2990091-X\u0022\u003E10.1016/0021-8693(69)90091-X\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca hre